		<elementInformation name="designation" show="1">EtherCAT Terminal, labels as drawn</elementInformation>
		<elementInformation name="description" show="1">EtherCAT Terminal, potential feed terminal. Pin names are the Beckhoff terminal points in the order of the user's own drawing (left column 1 to 4, right column 5 to 8): 1 END1, 2 NC1, 3 NC3, 4 NC5, 5 END2, 6 NC2, 7 NC4, 8 NC6. The channel is the signal in the I/O table, not the pin number. Check this against the datasheet of your terminal.</elementInformation>
	</elementInformations>
	<informations>Author: QElectroTech contributors
Generic layout, not copied from a manufacturer drawing. License: see http://qelectrotech.org/wiki/doc/elements_license
Schematic view made by misc/beckhoff/gen_schematic.py from the realistic view: the stages are generic, check them against the datasheet. License: see http://qelectrotech.org/wiki/doc/elements_license</informations>
